{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Work is performed on the existing open-source Spring XD codebase (Spring Integration / Spring for Apache Hadoop / Kafka message bus based), using its established module, stream DSL, and admin/REST endpoint architecture; no migration to Spring Framework 6 / Java 17 is in scope for this increment.",
    "U1: Remove the module list from BaseDefinition and lazily re-parse the DSL text on demand via the existing StreamParser, keeping the change backward compatible with persisted stream definitions.",
    "U2: Implement reliable HDFS writes by extending the existing HDFS sink (Spring for Apache Hadoop) with commit acknowledgement callbacks propagated back over the message bus, plus configuration options (e.g., enable/timeout/retry) and metrics.",
    "U3: Expose the partition key/expression as an overridable option on source and processor modules, resolved via SpEL against the message at runtime and passed to the message bus partition strategy.",
    "U4: Extend the Kafka message bus consumer configuration to support subscribing to a list of topic-partitions and merging them into the single inbound queue/channel of the module.",
    "U5: Extend the existing XD DSL parser into a context-aware parser endpoint that accepts prior stream definitions (symbol table) so partially parsed streams (as sent by the Flo UI) can be validated, including module/option value checks.",
    "U6: Produce a design document (spike) only: module colocation, classloader isolation, lifecycle and transport implications of deploying a whole stream in a single container; no production code delivered.",
    "U7: Centralize handling of non-default ConfigurableConversionService instances in the tuple serialization/deserialization path so custom conversion services survive Kryo/serialization round-trips.",
    "U8: Build a small repeatable benchmark harness (JMH-style or load-injection script) around a representative stream, run it with JMX enabled and disabled, and publish a results document.",
    "Testing uses the existing Spring XD test infrastructure: JUnit unit tests, Spring integration tests, and embedded/local Kafka and HDFS (mini-cluster) fixtures for integration tests.",
    "All code changes go through the standard GitHub fork/branch + pull request code review process before merge."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "One experienced developer (the estimator) performs all work; estimates are effort in workdays (1 workday = 8 productive hours), not calendar duration.",
    "The developer has full access to the Spring XD source code, build system, CI pipeline, and existing test fixtures, including local/embedded Kafka and HDFS mini-clusters.",
    "The referenced branch for U1 exists and contains the prior XD-2877 groundwork.",
    "Scope is limited to the eight user stories; each includes design, implementation, unit/integration testing, and minimal user/developer documentation as appropriate.",
    "U6 is a design-and-documentation spike only; implementation of single-container deployment is out of scope.",
    "U8 requires creating a lightweight benchmark harness but no new infrastructure procurement.",
    "Estimates exclude project management, release management, production deployment, and ongoing maintenance.",
    "No external blockers (e.g., unavailable reviewers, environment outages) are included; code review effort of the author is included, reviewer effort is excluded."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-01",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Analyze and design BaseDefinition refactor",
      "activity_description": "Review the existing branch and BaseDefinition usage, identify all consumers of the module list, and design the lazy re-parse approach.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-02",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Implement BaseDefinition module-list removal with on-demand reparse",
      "activity_description": "Refactor BaseDefinition to remove the persisted module list and reparse the DSL text as needed; update all affected callers.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-03",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Unit and integration tests for refactor",
      "activity_description": "Add/update tests covering stream definition parsing, equality, persistence round-trips, and regression tests for affected components.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-04",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Design reliable HDFS write acknowledgements",
      "activity_description": "Design commit-acknowledgement flow from HDFS sink back over the message bus, including options (timeout, retry), failure semantics, and metrics.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-05",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Implement reliable HDFS writes for stream pipelines",
      "activity_description": "Extend the HDFS sink with commit callbacks/sync semantics, configuration options, and acknowledgement propagation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-06",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Test reliable HDFS writes",
      "activity_description": "Unit tests plus integration tests against an HDFS mini-cluster, including failure/timeout scenarios and option validation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-07",
      "activity_name": "U3 - Implement partition function override in source/processor modules",
      "activity_description": "Add an overridable partition key/expression option resolved via SpEL and wired into the message bus partitioning strategy.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-08",
      "activity_name": "U3 - Test partition function override",
      "activity_description": "Unit and integration tests verifying custom partition expressions route messages to the expected partitions, including default behavior.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-09",
      "activity_name": "U4 - Implement consumption from multiple topic-partitions",
      "activity_description": "Extend the Kafka message bus consumer to subscribe to multiple topic-partitions and merge them into a single inbound queue/channel.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-10",
      "activity_name": "U4 - Test multi-partition consumption",
      "activity_description": "Integration tests against embedded Kafka verifying consumption from several partitions through a single queue, ordering expectations, and configuration validation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-11",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Design context-aware DSL parser endpoint",
      "activity_description": "Design parser API changes to accept known stream definitions as context so Flo's partial parses (e.g., taps referencing previously defined streams) validate correctly, including module/option value checks.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-12",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Implement new DSL parser for Flo integration",
      "activity_description": "Implement incremental/context-aware parsing, symbol resolution across streams, and validation of module/option values with clear error reporting.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-13",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Test DSL parser and endpoint",
      "activity_description": "Unit tests for parser grammar/validation and endpoint tests covering the Flo partial-parse scenarios and error messages.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-14",
      "activity_name": "U6 - Design and document single-container stream deployment",
      "activity_description": "Investigate and document the approach for colocating all modules of a stream in one container: classloading, lifecycle, transport bypass, configuration, and trade-offs.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-15",
      "activity_name": "U7 - Uniform handling of non-default ConfigurableConversionService in tuples",
      "activity_description": "Centralize conversion-service handling so custom services are not reset after tuple deserialization; includes regression tests for serialization round-trips.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-16",
      "activity_name": "U8 - Benchmark stream with and without JMX and document results",
      "activity_description": "Set up a repeatable benchmark harness for a representative stream, run with JMX enabled and disabled, analyze throughput/latency differences, and write the findings document.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-17",
      "activity_name": "Cross-cutting - Code review, rework and integration",
      "activity_description": "Author-side pull request preparation, addressing review feedback, rebasing branches, and resolving integration conflicts across the eight stories.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-18",
      "activity_name": "Cross-cutting - Final documentation and build/CI verification",
      "activity_description": "Update reference docs/release notes for new options and behaviors, and verify the full CI build and test suite pass for the increment.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 53
  }
}
```

